<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Wu of Chen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">503–559</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Chen Baxian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-han">Emperor Wu</a> of Chen, born Chen Baxian, was a Liang general who suppressed the rising of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ly-nam-de">Lý Bí</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> in 545 and helped defeat the rebel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hou-jing">Hou Jing</a>. Taking control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiankang">Jiankang</a>, he deposed the last Liang emperor in 557 and founded the Chen dynasty, the last of the southern dynasties before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s reunification under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-chen.jpg" alt="Emperor Wu of Chen" width="320" height="397" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emperor_Wu_of_Chen2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
